        "The maintainer stated that the fix will be included in future versions.",
        null,
        "This report is through a private channel (email). \nReport: In the file salt/salt/runners/digicertapi.py, the 3DES algorithm appears to be used to generate the private key for RSA. However, 3DES is no longer considered secure because of its limited effective key size and known vulnerabilities to block collision attacks. It is recommended to replace 3DES with a modern symmetric encryption algorithm such as AES-256. In the file salt/salt/utils/pycrypto.py, the MD5 hash function is supported in the project. MD5 has long been deprecated for security-sensitive operations due to its susceptibility to collision attacks, which can compromise data integrity and authentication. A more secure alternative such as SHA-256 or SHA-3 should be used instead. The same file also indicates support for DES. Like 3DES, DES is outdated and easily broken by brute-force attacks due to its short 56-bit key length. It should be removed from the project and replaced with a secure algorithm such as AES.\nResponse: We are aware of the current state of our crypto algorithms. There is an on-going effort to update them in the next major release of salt 3008.0. In the meantime, you are able to mitigate any potential risk by using a transport that supports TLS.",
