        "This report is through a private channel (email). \nReport: During a code review of the PyPDF project, it was observed that certain insecure cryptographic algorithms and modes are still implemented within the codebase. Specifically, ARC4 (RC4) and AES in ECB mode are present, both of which are regarded as cryptographically unsafe by current security standards.\n\nResponse:pypdf is designed to follow the official PDF specification, which unfortunately still includes some older and insecure cryptographic methods. Because of that, we have to support certain algorithms like ARC4 or AES in ECB mode — otherwise, we’d lose compatibility with existing PDF files. Automatic tools may flag these as insecure, but they’re part of the standard and can’t simply be removed.",
