        null,
        "efficiency",
        "This report is through a private channel (email). \nReport: A review of the XX-Net project’s source code revealed potential cryptographic weaknesses in the implementation. Specifically, the initialization vector used in rc4_wrap.py is statically defined as all zeros, which violates best practices for AES encryption that require a securely generated random IV to maintain confidentiality across encryption operations. Additionally, the encryption key is derived directly from the sni variable, introducing a potential lack of entropy and predictability in key generation. These design flaws may compromise the overall security of the encryption process and should be addressed to ensure compliance with modern cryptographic standards.\n\nResponse:we appreciate the feedback, the primary focus of the project remains ensuring reliable circumvention of the GFW. Decryption is already challenging, as most network traffic today is HTTPS-based. The best approach for improving security and effectiveness is to apply an additional encryption layer to all traffic before it enters any tunnel. To achieve this, the current protocol should be redesigned and upgraded accordingly.",
